# Testing Conventions

## Blackbox principle

- Tests expose bugs — do not weaken assertions to greenwash failures.
- Fix production code when behavior is wrong; change tests only for wrong expectations or intentional contract changes.
- See also: `.cursor/failing-tests-debugging.mdc`

## Unit / component (Vitest)

- Live under `tests/`, mirroring `src/` (e.g. `tests/lib/api.test.ts`, `tests/pages/LoginPage.test.tsx`)
- Use `@testing-library/react`, `@testing-library/user-event`, `@testing-library/jest-dom`
- Import app code via `@/` (e.g. `@/lib/api`, `@/pages/LoginPage`)
- Mock `fetch` for API calls; use `MemoryRouter` for routed pages
- See `tests/lib/api.test.ts` for patterns

```bash
npm test -- --run
npm test -- --run tests/lib/api.test.ts
```

## E2E (Playwright)

- Specs in `tests/e2e/` (auth, tags, facts); helpers in `tests/e2e/helpers.ts`
- Auth via `localStorage` key `wordupx_token` (see `tests/e2e/global-setup.ts`)
- CI runs Chromium with secrets `E2E_USERNAME`, `E2E_PASSWORD`

```bash
E2E_USERNAME=... E2E_PASSWORD=... npm run test:e2e
npm run test:e2e:ui
```
